    {
      "finding": "Prepared root/ancestor aliases can write through to frozen input",
      "status": "passed",
      "implementation": "Reject root/ancestor/child symlinks and shared file inodes; exclusively create fresh owned copies and independently verify inode/bytes; adapter only writes inspected owned inodes via no-follow handles. Metadata writes reject leaf aliases.",
      "evidence": "Positive independent copy/write plus root, ancestor, child, hardlink and metadata alias regressions; actual responsive CLI rejects aliased prepared roots before touching source. Original parent inputs byte/inode comparisons remain equal; separately prepared public workspace equals local preview bytes with different inodes."
    },
